BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:minior-showers-orionids-2026@pokemon-go-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261106T105116Z
SUMMARY:Minior Showers: Orionids 2026
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Lisbon:20261019T170000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Lisbon:20261024T235900
DESCRIPTION:Explore by starlight during the Orionids meteor shower for a ch
 ance to encounter Minior in Pokémon GO!\nThis Minior Shower runs from Oct
 ober 19\, 2026 at 5:00 p.m. to October 24\, 2026 at 11:59 p.m. local time.
 \n\n━━ BONUSES ━━\n• 1\,000 Stardust for catching Minior\n• In
 creased chance to encounter Minior from 5:00 p.m. to 9:00 p.m. local time 
 each day\n\n━━ FEATURES ━━\n▸ Pokémon Debut\nMinior (Green Core
 )\, the Meteor Pokémon\, will make its Pokémon GO debut during the Orion
 ids meteor shower\, beginning October 19\, 2026\, at 5:00 p.m. local time!
 \nMinior has seven different core colors: Red\, Orange\, Yellow\, Green\, 
 Blue\, Indigo\, and Violet. A different core color will debut during each 
 of the six meteor showers listed below. During the Geminids\, one core col
 or will debut in the Northern Hemisphere and another in the Southern Hemis
 phere.\nPokémon: Minior (Green Core)\nGreen Core Minior debuts during the
  Orionids. The core colors for the remaining meteor showers have not been 
 announced.\n\n▸ Explore by Starlight\nFrom 5:00 p.m. to 9:00 p.m. local 
 time every day during each Minior Shower\, shooting stars will light up th
 e in-game sky. During these hours\, you’ll have an increased chance of e
 ncountering Minior in the wild!\n\n▸ Minior’s Form Changes\nMinior beg
 ins battles in its Meteor Form. When its health drops below 50%\, it chang
 es form and exposes its core.\n• Meteor Form: Higher Defense and lower A
 ttack.\n• Core exposed: Higher Attack and lower Defense.\nInitially\, Mi
 nior will only be able to change forms when battling Team GO Rocket\, team
  leaders\, or in the GO Battle League.\nMinior will not be eligible for th
 e 2027 Latin America International Championships.\n\n▸ Annual Meteor Sho
 wer Schedule\nMinior can appear during the following meteor showers each y
 ear. Each shower begins at 5:00 p.m. on its first day and ends at 11:59 p.
 m. on its last day\, in local time.\n• Orionids: October 19–24\, 2026\
 n• Leonids: November 14–19\, 2026\n• Geminids: December 11–16\, 20
 26\n• Eta Aquariids: May 3–8\, 2027\n• Southern Delta Aquariids: Jul
 y 28–August 2\, 2027\n• Perseids: August 10–15\, 2027\n\n━━ SPAW
 NS ━━\n▸ Wild Encounters\nYou may encounter Minior in its Meteor For
 m in the wild during the event. You’ll receive 1\,000 Stardust for catch
 ing Minior.\nPokémon: Minior (Meteor Form)\nMinior encounters are more li
 kely from 5:00 p.m. to 9:00 p.m. local time each day.\n\n━━ RESEARCH 
 ━━\nTimed Research will be available during the event. Claim a Star Pi
 ece\, then complete five Use a Star Piece tasks to earn 7\,740 Stardust ea
 ch. Complete all tasks to earn an additional 77\,400 Stardust.\nSome very 
 lucky Trainers will receive this Bonus Timed Research. Claim a Star Piece\
 , then use a Star Piece to earn 774 Stardust and a completion reward of 1\
 ,000\,000 Stardust!\nTimed Research tasks must be completed and all reward
 s claimed by October 24\, 2026\, at 11:59 p.m. local time.\n\n🔗 https:/
 /leekduck.com/events/minior-showers-orionids-2026/
URL:https://leekduck.com/events/minior-showers-orionids-2026/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:gbl-twilight-trails_ultra-league_master-league-mega-edition_fantasy-cup
 -great-league-edition@pokemon-go-calendar
