BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pokemon-go-wild-area-2026-global@pokemon-go-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261106T105116Z
SUMMARY:Pokémon GO Wild Area 2026: Global
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Lisbon:20261114T100000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Lisbon:20261115T180000
DESCRIPTION:GO Wild Area returns in 2026 with Steel- and Dragon-type Pokém
 on\, the debuts of Gigantamax Duraludon\, Dynamax Dialga\, and Dynamax Pal
 kia\, and powerful mighty Pokémon. Collect GO Safari Balls to help catch 
 these challenging encounters!\nDates: November 14 and 15\, 2026 Time: 10:0
 0 a.m. – 6:00 p.m. local time each day Location: Worldwide\nAll Trainers
  can participate in the global event. An optional US$11.99 ticket adds Spe
 cial Research\, increased Shiny chances\, extra Incense encounters\, and a
 dditional bonuses across both days. Purchase a ticket from the Pokémon GO
  Web Store.\n\n▸ Related Events\n\n━━ BONUSES ━━\n▸ Bonuses fo
 r All Trainers\nThe following bonuses apply from 10:00 a.m. to 6:00 p.m. l
 ocal time on both event days.\n• Chance to get GO Safari Balls from Pok
 éStops and Gyms\n• Up to 3 free Raid Passes per day from Gyms\n• Dail
 y Max Particle collection limit increased to 1\,600\n• 3 GO Snapshot sur
 prise encounters per day\n• Party Play lasts for 8 hours\n• Chance to 
 encounter mighty Pokémon on Routes\nDaily Discoveries will be paused from
  November 9 at 12:01 a.m. through November 15\, 2026\, at 11:59 p.m. local
  time.\n\n▸ Additional Ticket Holder Bonuses\nThese benefits apply from 
 10:00 a.m. to 6:00 p.m. local time on both event days. The ticketed Raid P
 ass and Max Particle limits replace the free limits.\n• Increased chance
  to encounter Shiny Pokémon\n• Daily Max Particle collection limit incr
 eased to 3\,200\n• Increased Max Particles from Power Spots and explorat
 ion\n• Up to 6 free Raid Passes per day from Gyms\n• 2× Candy for cat
 ching Pokémon\n• 2× Incense duration\n• Increased chance of 10 km Eg
 gs from PokéStops and Gyms\n• 6 GO Snapshot surprise encounters per day
 \n• Lure Modules last for 2 hours\n\n▸ Trading Bonuses\nTicket holders
  receive these benefits from 12:00 a.m. to 11:59 p.m. local time on both e
 vent days.\n• Up to 6 Special Trades per day\n• 1/2 Stardust cost for 
 trades\nShiny encounters are not guaranteed. To use the increased explorat
 ion Max Particle bonus\, first collect all available Max Particles in the 
 Nearby menu. Adventure Sync can help track exploration distance.\n\n━━
  FEATURES ━━\n▸ Gigantamax Duraludon Debuts\nGigantamax Duraludon ma
 kes its Pokémon GO debut at Pokémon GO Wild Area! This larger-than-life 
 Pokémon will appear in six-star Max Battles during the event.\nTicket-hol
 ding Trainers can learn more about Gigantamax Duraludon in the event-exclu
 sive Special Research story. Complete it for an encounter with Gigantamax 
 Duraludon with a Special Background!\nIf you’re lucky\, you may encounte
 r a Shiny one!\nPokémon: Gigantamax Duraludon\n\n▸ Dynamax Dialga and D
 ynamax Palkia\nDynamax Dialga and Dynamax Palkia make their Pokémon GO de
 buts during GO Wild Area 2026. Both can be Shiny!\nFor Global\, Dynamax Di
 alga appears on Saturday\, November 14\, and Dynamax Palkia appears on Sun
 day\, November 15.\n\n▸ Private Dynamax Battle Groups\nStarting with GO 
 Wild Area 2026\, Dynamax Battle lobbies offer Battle to match automaticall
 y with other Trainers or Private Group to join an existing group using its
  group code.\n\n▸ Adventure Effects in Battle Lobbies\nStarting with Int
 o the Wild\, select Adventure Effects can be activated while waiting in a 
 raid or Max Battle lobby. Use Crowned Sword Zacian’s Behemoth Blade or C
 rowned Shield Zamazenta’s Behemoth Bash Adventure Effect before a Max Ba
 ttle to help your group.\n\n▸ Machamp Wearing a Modern Jacket\nA new cos
 tumed Machamp appears in three-star raids during the event. Lucky Trainers
  may encounter a Shiny one!\n\n▸ Special Backgrounds\nAfter a successful
  catch from raids or Max Battles\, Machamp wearing a modern jacket\, Dynam
 ax Dialga\, Dynamax Palkia\, Reshiram\, Zekrom\, Kyurem\, and Gigantamax D
 uraludon have a chance to have a new Special Background.\n\n▸ Background
 s on Your Trainer Profile\nYour buddy Pokémon’s eligible Location Backg
 round or Special Background can now appear on your Trainer profile\, where
  friends can see it too. Background support rolls out on the following sch
 edule:\n• November 6\, 2026\, at 10:00 a.m. local time: GO Wild Area 202
 6 Location Backgrounds for Sendai and Mexico City.\n…\n\n━━ SPAWNS 
 ━━\n▸ Rotating Habitat Hours\nSteel- and Dragon-themed encounters ro
 tate hourly from 10:00 a.m. to 6:00 p.m. on both event days.\n\n▸ Solid 
 as Steel Hour\n10:00 a.m. to 11:00 a.m. 12:00 p.m. to 1:00 p.m. 2:00 p.m. 
 to 3:00 p.m. 4:00 p.m. to 5:00 p.m.\nPokémon: Alolan Sandshrew\, Alolan D
 iglett\, Magnemite\, Shellder\, Onix\, Porygon\, Shuckle\, Skarmory\, Nose
 pass\, Aron\, Beldum\, Piplup\, Shieldon\, Bronzor\, Lucario\, Drilbur\, F
 erroseed\, Klink\, Galarian Stunfisk\, Durant\, Rookidee\, Tinkatink\n\n
 ▸ Daring as Dragons Hour\n11:00 a.m. to 12:00 p.m. 1:00 p.m. to 2:00 p.m
 . 3:00 p.m. to 4:00 p.m. 5:00 p.m. to 6:00 p.m.\nPokémon: Charmander\, Ma
 gikarp\, Dratini\, Gligar\, Trapinch\, Swablu\, Barboach\, Bagon\, Gible\,
  Tynamo\, Axew\, Heatmor\, Deino\, Skrelp\, Tyrunt\, Amaura\, Goomy\, Noib
 at\, Turtonator\, Jangmo-o\, Sizzlipede\, Frigibax\n\n▸ Mighty Pokémon\
 nMighty Pokémon are more likely to have high Attack\, Defense\, and HP ra
 tings and be XL or XXL. They are harder to catch\, and some may be Shiny. 
 GO Safari Balls improve your chances of catching them.\nThe wild mighty Po
 kémon lineup changes each day.\n\n▸ Saturday\, November 14\nPokémon: A
 lolan Exeggutor\, Scizor\, Flygon\, Walrein\, Metagross\, Empoleon\, Magne
 zone\, Conkeldurr\, Haxorus\n\n▸ Sunday\, November 15\nPokémon: Azumari
 ll\, Kingdra\, Aggron\, Ferrothorn\, Hydreigon\, Goodra\, Noivern\, Tinkat
 on\, Clodsire\n\n▸ Incense Encounters\nAll Trainers can attract these mi
 ghty Pokémon on both event days. These encounters exclude Daily Adventure
  Incense.\nPokémon: Alolan Exeggutor\, Azumarill\, Scizor\, Kingdra\, Agg
 ron\, Flygon\, Empoleon\, Magnezone\, Conkeldurr\, Hydreigon\n\n▸ Ticket
  Holder Incense Encounters\nTicket holders can also attract the following 
 Unown on both days.\nPokémon: Unown D\, Unown I\, Unown L\, Unown W\nLuck
 y ticket holders may also encounter these mighty Legendary Pokémon from I
 ncense:\n…\n\n━━ EGGS ━━\n…
URL:https://leekduck.com/events/pokemon-go-wild-area-2026-global/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:minior-showers-leonids-2026@pokemon-go-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261106T105116Z
SUMMARY:Minior Showers: Leonids 2026
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Lisbon:20261114T170000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Lisbon:20261119T235900
DESCRIPTION:Explore by starlight during the Leonids meteor shower for a cha
 nce to encounter Minior in Pokémon GO!\nThis Minior Shower runs from Nove
 mber 14\, 2026 at 5:00 p.m. to November 19\, 2026 at 11:59 p.m. local time
 .\n\n━━ BONUSES ━━\n• Increased Stardust for catching Minior\n
 • Increased chance to encounter Minior from 5:00 p.m. to 9:00 p.m. local
  time each day\n\n━━ FEATURES ━━\n▸ Minior Cores\nMinior has sev
 en different core colors: Red\, Orange\, Yellow\, Green\, Blue\, Indigo\, 
 and Violet. A different core color will debut during each of the six meteo
 r showers listed below. During the Geminids\, one core color will debut in
  the Northern Hemisphere and another in the Southern Hemisphere.\nPokémon
 : Minior (Red Core)\, Minior (Orange Core)\, Minior (Yellow Core)\, Minior
  (Green Core)\, Minior (Blue Core)\, Minior (Indigo Core)\, Minior (Violet
  Core)\nGreen Core Minior debuts during the Orionids. The core colors for 
 the remaining meteor showers have not been announced.\n\n▸ Explore by St
 arlight\nFrom 5:00 p.m. to 9:00 p.m. local time every day during each Mini
 or Shower\, shooting stars will light up the in-game sky. During these hou
 rs\, you’ll have an increased chance of encountering Minior in the wild!
 \n\n▸ Minior’s Form Changes\nMinior begins battles in its Meteor Form.
  When its health drops below 50%\, it changes form and exposes its core.\n
 • Meteor Form: Higher Defense and lower Attack.\n• Core exposed: Highe
 r Attack and lower Defense.\nInitially\, Minior will only be able to chang
 e forms when battling Team GO Rocket\, team leaders\, or in the GO Battle 
 League.\nMinior will not be eligible for the 2027 Latin America Internatio
 nal Championships.\n\n▸ Annual Meteor Shower Schedule\nMinior can appear
  during the following meteor showers each year. Each shower begins at 5:00
  p.m. on its first day and ends at 11:59 p.m. on its last day\, in local t
 ime.\n• Orionids: October 19–24\, 2026\n• Leonids: November 14–19\
 , 2026\n• Geminids: December 11–16\, 2026\n• Eta Aquariids: May 3–
 8\, 2027\n• Southern Delta Aquariids: July 28–August 2\, 2027\n• Per
 seids: August 10–15\, 2027\n\n━━ SPAWNS ━━\n▸ Wild Encounters\
 nYou may encounter Minior in its Meteor Form in the wild during the event.
  You’ll receive 1\,000 Stardust for catching Minior.\nPokémon: Minior (
 Meteor Form)\nMinior encounters are more likely from 5:00 p.m. to 9:00 p.m
 . local time each day.\n\n🔗 https://leekduck.com/events/minior-showers-
 leonids-2026/
URL:https://leekduck.com/events/minior-showers-leonids-2026/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
