BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:dynamax-trails-2026@pokemon-go-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261106T105116Z
SUMMARY:Dynamax Trails
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Lisbon:20261116T100000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Lisbon:20261123T200000
DESCRIPTION:Get ready for a week of Max Battles! Dynamax Pokémon return\, 
 Max Particles are surging in the wild\, and Eternamax Eternatus returns to
  Power Spots during Dynamax Trails.\nThe Dynamax Trails event will take pl
 ace from November 16\, 2026 at 10 am to November 23\, 2026 at 8 pm local t
 ime.\n\n▸ Related Events\n\n━━ BONUSES ━━\nThe following bonuses
  will be active during the event.\n• Chance to receive Max Particles whe
 n catching event-themed Pokémon in the wild or after Max Battles\n• Mor
 e Power Spots than usual will be active\nMax Particles cannot be obtained 
 from catches with the Explorer Gadget or a Pokémon GO Plus +.\n\n━━ F
 EATURES ━━\n▸ Max Battles\nAll Dynamax Pokémon that have previously
  appeared in Pokémon GO may appear in Max Battles during the event\, excl
 uding Legendary and Mythical Pokémon.\n\n▸ Special Background\nAfter su
 ccessfully catching a Pokémon from a Max Battle during the event\, Traine
 rs will have a chance to receive a Special Background. It appears on the P
 okémon’s summary page to commemorate when it was caught.\n\n▸ Eternat
 us Returns\nEternamax Eternatus will take over the majority of Power Spots
  on November 21\, 2026\, from 11 am to 2 pm local time.\nPokémon: Eternam
 ax Eternatus\nTrainers cannot catch Eternamax Eternatus after defeating it
  in Max Battles. Instead\, they will earn a large amount of Eternatus Cand
 y and Eternatus Candy XL to power up Eternatus obtained through GO Pass: D
 ynamax Trails.\nDuring this window\, Power Spots will refresh more frequen
 tly\, the Max Particle collection limit will increase to 2\,400\, and Powe
 r Spots will award 8× Max Particles.\nThe daily Remote Raid limit will in
 crease from 10 to 30 from November 20 at 1 pm to November 21 at 6 pm PST (
 GMT −8).\nView the Eternamax Eternatus event details.\n\n▸ Spotlight H
 our\nGrookey\, Scorbunny\, and Sobble will be featured during Pokémon Spo
 tlight Hour on November 19\, 2026\, from 6 pm to 7 pm local time. The bonu
 s will be 2× Catch Candy.\nPokémon: Grookey\, Scorbunny\, Sobble\n\n▸ 
 Event-Themed Stickers\nGet event-themed stickers by spinning PokéStops\, 
 opening Gifts\, purchasing them from the in-game shop\, and progressing th
 rough your GO Pass.\n\n━━ SPAWNS ━━\n▸ Wild Encounters\nEvent-th
 emed Pokémon will appear in the wild\, including any Pokémon that has de
 buted in Dynamax Max Battles\, excluding Legendary and Mythical Pokémon.\
 n\n━━ RESEARCH ━━\n▸ Field Research Task Rewards\nComplete event
 -themed Field Research tasks to earn Stardust\, Eternatus Candy\, encounte
 rs with event-themed Pokémon\, and more.\n\n━━ GO PASS ━━\n▸ GO
  Pass: Dynamax Trails\nGO Pass is a free\, limited-time progression track.
  Collect GO Points and complete Pass Tasks to rank up and earn rewards.\nT
 rainers will automatically receive GO Pass: Dynamax Trails on November 16\
 , 2026\, at 10 am local time. GO Points can be collected through November 
 23\, 2026\, at 8 pm local time.\nTrainers who claim Tier 1 rewards (Rank 2
 5) on GO Pass: Into the Wild will receive early access on November 14\, 20
 26\, at 10 am local time\, and a free upgrade to GO Pass Deluxe: Dynamax T
 rails.\nGO Pass Deluxe is also available for US$4.99 (or the equivalent pr
 icing tier in your local currency)\, offering upgraded rewards and faster 
 progression. Deluxe Trainers can claim rewards from both tracks\, includin
 g rewards from ranks unlocked before upgrading.\nClaim all unlocked reward
 s by November 25\, 2026\, at 8 pm local time\, before they expire.\n\n▸ 
 Featured Pokémon and Rewards\nComplete Pass Tasks to earn:\n• Encounter
 s with event-themed Dynamax Pokémon with a Special Background\n• An enc
 ounter with Eternatus\, or 100 Eternatus Candy if you have already caught 
 Eternatus\n• Eternatus Candy and Candy XL\n• Rare Candy\n• Stardust\
 n• Event-themed stickers\n• Additional rewards\nPokémon: Eternatus\nE
 ternatus can only be caught once during this event and requires much more 
 Candy and Candy XL to power up due to its massive power. Trainers who have
  already caught Eternatus will receive Candy to continue powering it up.\n
 GO Pass Deluxe also offers:\n• Additional encounters with event-themed D
 ynamax Pokémon with a Special Background\n• More Eternatus Candy and Ca
 ndy XL\n• Silver Pinap Berries\n• Rare Candy XL\n• Event-themed stic
 kers\n• Additional rewards\n\n▸ Major Milestone Bonuses\nReach the fol
 lowing ranks on your event GO Pass to unlock these bonuses.\n\n▸ Tier 1:
  Rank 15\n…\n\n🔗 https://leekduck.com/events/dynamax-trails-2026/
URL:https://leekduck.com/events/dynamax-trails-2026/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
